"body": "Fellow Greymanes,\nHere are the fixes and improvements that have been added this patch.\n\n## Update Schedule\n\nPlease refer to the Updates section below to see the state of the patch for each platform.\n\n### Update\n\nSteam (PC): Patch available now\nSteam (Mac): Patch available now\nPlayStation: Patch available now\nXbox: Patch available now\nXbox on PC: Patch available now\nEpic Games Store: Patch available now\nMac App Store: Patch available now\n\n## Patch Details\n\nTemplate Start\nTemplate End\n- Improved the game so that changes to the Minimum Font Size settings are applied immediately.\n- Fixed an issue where starting a new game while a separate save file existed applied a game difficulty setting apart from the one actually selected.\n- Fixed an issue where some parts of the Guides UI were disabled.\n- Fixed an issue where parts of the fishing dock vendor's and tanner's shop UI were displayed awkwardly.\n- Fixed an issue where changing a Pet's name would change the name of a non-Pet animal in the trust increase notifications.\n- [Keyboard/Mouse] Fixed an issue where key inputs would not work while adjusting Others > Video > HDR.\n- Fixed an issue where, when the Extra Rewards List and Content Guide UIs overlapped, the Content UI in the back would be interacted with first.\n- Fixed an issue where the fadeout in some shop cutscenes occurred too slowly.\n- Fixed an issue where horse gear could not be dyed.\n- Fixed various localization errors across all languages.\n- Slightly increased character movement speed. (This change was applied in Patch Version 1.04.00)\n- [PlayStation 5 Pro] Fixed an issue where screen brightness would become unstable when \"PSSR Sharpness\" was enabled.\n- Added a Greymane Contribution Shop with Carl at the Greymane Camp. (This change was applied in Patch Version 1.04.00.)\n- When expanding the camp, furniture placed in the house will no longer be retrieved. (This change was applied in Patch Version 1.04.00)\n  - However, if the house layout is changed through housing mode, all placed furniture will be retrieved.\n- Improved the Greymane Camp. (To avoid spoilers, changes related to this content are listed in the dropdown menu below.) When relocating the Greymane Camp to Pailune, furniture placed in the house will now be moved together as well. (This change was applied in Patch Version 1.04.00)\n\n## Known Issues\n\n- For known issues, please check the notice below:\n  - [[Crimson Desert Known Issues]](https://crimsondesert.pearlabyss.com/News/Notice/Detail?_boardNo=68)\nTemplate Start\nTemplate End\nTemplate BTN - Big Parchment Start [버튼 배경 이미지 ![](https://s1.pearlcdn.com/cd/brand/contents_cd/img/main/btn_main.png)FAQ](https://crimsondesert.pearlabyss.com/News/Notice/Detail?_boardNo=63)[![](https://s1.pearlcdn.com/cd/brand/contents_cd/img/main/btn_main.png)Report an Issue](https://pearlabyss.info/crimsondesertreport)\nTemplate BTN - Big Parchment End\nWe are truly rooting for the journey that awaits you in Pywel.\nThank you!"
